+# Coverstore archival
+
+Coverstore stores new images under `data_root/localdisk/` and records their paths in
+`cover.filename`, `cover.filename_s`, `cover.filename_m`, and `cover.filename_l`.
+The archival process groups images into ZIP files under `data_root/items/`, uploads
+those files to Internet Archive, verifies the upload, and then records their
+archive.org download URLs in the same four columns.
+
+## ID and path schema
+
+A cover ID is formatted as a **10-digit, zero-padded decimal number**. The first
+four digits form the `item_id`; each item spans 1,000,000 IDs. The next two
+digits form the `batch_id`; each batch spans 10,000 IDs. The final four digits
+identify the cover within its batch. Use the same scheme for every ID range.
+
+For example, cover `8123456` becomes `0008123456`: item `0008`, batch `12`.
+Item IDs are always four digits and batch IDs are always two digits, including
+leading zeroes.
+
+| Size | Size prefix | Filename suffix | Database column |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Original (`''`) | `''` | `''` | `filename` |
+| Small (`s`) | `s_` | `-S` | `filename_s` |
+| Medium (`m`) | `m_` | `-M` | `filename_m` |
+| Large (`l`) | `l_` | `-L` | `filename_l` |
+
+For each size, the Internet Archive item and its batch ZIP are named:
+
+```text
+item:      <size_prefix>covers_<item_id>
+ZIP:       <size_prefix>covers_<item_id>_<batch_id>.zip
+on disk:   <data_root>/items/<size_prefix>covers_<item_id>/<size_prefix>covers_<item_id>_<batch_id>.zip
+inside ZIP: <10-digit-cover-id><filename-suffix>.<ext>
+URL:       <protocol>://archive.org/download/<item>/<ZIP>/<inside-ZIP-filename>
 ```
